From fa45a7210fbc675c5507a4cc76c18d6594c7e152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Elliott <mastacontrola@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:40:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Add IPv6 (dual-stack) to the socket layer and the
 protocol

udpcast was IPv4 only. Addresses are now sockaddr_storage, and the
helpers switch on the address family. A session is IPv6 when the
rendezvous address, the data address or the interface is IPv6. IPv4
sessions put the same defined bytes on the wire as before.

IPv6 uses IPV6_JOIN_GROUP, IPV6_MULTICAST_IF and IPV6_MULTICAST_HOPS
(from --ttl). IPv6 has no broadcast, so the default rendezvous is
ff02::1. The default data group is ff15::7564:0:<low 32 bits of the
sender address>. Interfaces are found with getifaddrs(). Scoped text
such as fe80::1%eth0 is accepted. Without IPv6 support from the
platform (UDPC_IPV6 unset), the build stays IPv4 only.

Upstream: not yet submitted

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
